   <name>Flood Advisory issued October 3 at 8:01PM EDT until October 3 at 10:00PM EDT by NWS Wilmington NC</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_minor</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.

* WHERE...Northern Robeson County in southeastern North Carolina...

* WHEN...Until 1000 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 801 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to slow
moving showers. Minor flooding is likely occurring in the
advisory area. Up to 5 inches of rain have fallen.
- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over the
area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Red Springs, Maxton, St. Pauls, Shannon, Buie, Rex, Prospect,
Wakulla, Tolarsville, Parkton, Rennert and Lumber Bridge.
- weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
