   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...For the first Small Craft Advisory, southeast winds 25
to 30 kt with gusts up to 40 kt and seas 8 to 13 ft. For the
Gale Warning, southeast winds 35 to 40 kt with gusts up to 45
kt and seas 11 to 16 ft expected. For the second Small Craft
Advisory, south winds 20 to 30 kt with gusts up to 45 kt and
seas 14 to 19 ft expected.

* WHERE...Cape Edgecumbe to Cape Spencer out to 15 NM.

* WHEN...For the first Small Craft Advisory, until 6 PM AKDT
this evening. For the Gale Warning, from 6 PM to 10 PM AKDT
this evening. For the second Small Craft Advisory, from 10 PM
this evening to 6 PM AKDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous seas which could
capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.</Snippet>
