   <Snippet>* WHAT...For the first Small Craft Advisory, east winds 25 to 30
kt with gusts up to 45 kt and seas 10 to 15 ft. For the Gale
Warning, east winds 35 to 40 kt and seas 14 to 19 ft expected.
For the second Small Craft Advisory, southeast winds 15 to 25
kt with gusts up to 40 kt and seas 15 to 20 ft expected.

* WHERE...Cape Fairweather to Icy Cape out to 15 NM.

* WHEN...For the first Small Craft Advisory, until 6 PM AKDT
this evening. For the Gale Warning, from 6 PM this evening to
1 AM AKDT Sunday. For the second Small Craft Advisory, from 1
AM to 6 PM AKDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous seas which could
capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.</Snippet>
