   <Snippet>...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in
Missouri...

Grand River near Chillicothe affecting Livingston and Linn
Counties.

Platte River near Agency affecting Buchanan County.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.

* WHERE...Platte River near Agency.

* WHEN...Until Monday afternoon.

* IMPACTS...At 20.0 feet, Low-lying areas east of Agency begin to
flood. At 25.0 feet, Flooding begins at the east border of Agency.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 12:30 PM CDT Saturday the stage was 25.0 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage early
tomorrow afternoon and continue falling to 8.1 feet Thursday
morning.
- Flood stage is 20.0 feet.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
